      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:9398825a57588c7a",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for to book in advance, then the Tamil for to apply."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: தட்டச்சு செய்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தட்டச்சு செய் — taṭṭaccu cey — \"to type\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தட்டச்சு செய் (taṭṭaccu cey) is a modern coinage from native words: taṭṭu, \"to tap, to strike\", accu, \"mould, type\" (DEDR 47, which lists Malayalam accu and Telugu accu 'print'), and sey, \"to do\" (DEDR 1957). DEDR itself compares accu, with a query, to Sanskrit sañcaka, \"mould\", so a link with Indo-Aryan is possible."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
